<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $26.49 bln on Apr 11.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $26.49 bln on Apr 11.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $26.49 billon on April 11, up from $26.37 billion a week ago, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  April 11     Apr 4	  Apr 12</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     22,435	22,313	 17,158</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,054	 4,054	  4,561</p>
<p>    SDRs				     2	     2	     42</p>
<p>    Total			     26,491	26,369	 21,761</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
